          "title": "You'll want to know: مخيم",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مخيم — mukhayyam — \"a campsite; a camp\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "كان المخيم بجانب البحيرة. kāna al-mukhayyam bi-jānib al-buḥayra. The campsite was beside the lake."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مخيم (mukhayyam) is built on the native Arabic root kh-y-m, \"a tent\" (Lane). It is the Form II passive participle: a place set with tents."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
